  "self_load_only": true,
  "description": "bigville R71 (block 388000): CONTAINERS -- a class of the same kind as PILE. A Pile is loose matter (kind, qty); a Container (a barrel, sack, bucket, bin, chest, safe) is the sibling class: a physical, located, claimable world-fact too, but with a CAPACITY that holds CONTENTS (cont -contains-> inner pile). ct_fill moves matter from a loose pile INTO a container up to its remaining room (never overfilled); ct_empty takes it back out -- both by ACCESS (co-location), both CONSERVED. Unifies the safe (coins in a locked container) and the Larder (cold store). Composes with the physical pile model (387000: piles are world-facts, ownership is recognized). Deferred: discrete containment (a chest of tool ITEMS via contains-edges); a lock+key gating access to a container (the safe); per-content ownership vs owning the vessel. LOCK+KEY: a container may be lockable (locked, lock_id); access (fill/empty) requires it be unlocked OR the agent hold a key that opens it -- a SAFE is a locked container. ck_lock/ck_unlock: a keyholder locks/unlocks. Composes with bigville_coin_safe.",
