    {
      "name": "ct_fill",
      "batch": false,
      "comment": "FILLING a container (by ACCESS): an agent AT a place, a loose pile AT the place, and a container AT the place holding an inner pile of the SAME kind -- move min(fill_amount, loose.qty, remaining room) from the loose pile into the container. Bounded by CAPACITY (never overfilled); matter is MOVED not created (conserved). A container is a peer of a pile -- both located world-facts -- but it has capacity and CONTAINS. (moved is stashed first, then applied to both sides -- avoids the sequential-read lag.) LOCK: only if the container is unlocked, or the agent holds a key that opens it (a locked safe blocks access without the key).",
